 82		The following data exhibit $L_{\mathsf{ALine}}$ as a $2$-level conditionally linear function. Its first level is the projection of $V$ onto the coordinate register $V_I$, which is linear. For a first-level value with coordinate component $s$, its second level is the linear map $L^{\mathrm{Ln}}_{e_i}$ with $i = \chi(s)$, acting on the point register $V_X$. The registers $V_I$ and $V_X$ are disjoint, so the second level is supported on a register subspace disjoint from the first, and summing the two contributions gives $\bigl(L^{\mathrm{Ln}}_{e_i}(u),\, s,\, 0\bigr)$, which is $L_{\mathsf{ALine}}(u,s,v)$ by Equation~\eqref{eq:cl-alnf}.
